id: pm-0k19l7
title: "pm get silently discards --output-include field names because entity reads bind the flag to sections while collection reads bind it to fields, and the omission receipt reports no omissions either way"
description: "One documented flag addresses two disjoint namespaces depending on the shape of the read. On pm get a field name matches nothing and is dropped with no diagnostic, so the highest-frequency read in the agent loop has no working field projection; mixing a section name with field names drops the item entity entirely. Both paths report omission_receipt.has_omissions false."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:contracts",output-contract,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-07T11:16:55.129Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T11:19:55.402Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "The namespace of --output-include is declared once in the output contract and is identical across entity and collection reads; Field projection works on pm get: requesting id and title returns an item carrying id and title, and the token receipt reflects the reduction; An --output-include token that matches neither a declared field nor a declared section is refused with a recovery hint naming the valid vocabulary for that command, rather than discarded; Mixing section and field names is either supported with defined precedence or refused; it can never silently drop the entity the read exists to return; The omission receipt reports every field and section withheld by an --output-include selection, and a conformance test asserts receipt-versus-payload agreement on both read shapes"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "One flag spelling means one thing on every read surface, and anything withheld is declared"
value: "The cheapest question an agent can ask about one item becomes cheap, and a projection that did not happen stops looking like one that did"
why_now: Token budgets are being promoted to the contract layer; a projection flag that no-ops silently will be inherited by every budget built on top of it
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
expected_result: "A field name passed to --output-include either projects that field on every read shape, or is refused with a message naming the correct flag; anything withheld appears in the omission receipt"
actual_result: On entity reads field names are silently discarded and the full entity is billed; adding a section name to the list drops the item entity; omission_receipt.has_omissions is false in both cases
